WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.480
- [Instructor] Each of these
pins is a Bed Bath &amp; Beyond

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.370
that closed in 2022.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.130
That's about 20% of its stores.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.830
Shares are at their lowest
point since the '90s

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.630
after the company said it's facing.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.250
- Bankruptcy.
- Bankruptcy.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.150
- Bankruptcy

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.470
- [Narrator] As sales collapsed,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.110
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond scrambled to cut costs

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.740
by laying off workers
and closing those stores.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.750
Here's what happened
to the home goods chain

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.730
in the last six months that led

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.693
to a cash crisis, and a
potential bankruptcy filing.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.270
Let's turn back the clock to June

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.230
when Bed Bath &amp; Beyond CEO
Mark Tritton had a problem.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.660
His strategy of scaling back coupons

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.300
and doing away with
popular national brands

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.910
in favor of private labels was failing.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.070
- [Mark] These are some of my
favorites from the Haven line.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.260
- [Narrator] And the company
was struggling to stock shelves

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.410
since it had fallen behind
on payments to vendors.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.160
Sales had fallen by 25%
compared to the previous year,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.253
and net losses were up
to over $350 million.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.500
On June 29th, the company
announced a leadership change.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.000
- [Harriet] Sue Gove has been named

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.550
interim chief executive officer,

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.940
replacing Mark Tritton,
who is leaving the company.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:12.773
- [Narrator] At the time,

00:01:12.773 --> 00:01:14.790
Gove said that Bed Bath &amp; Beyond's.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.910
- [Sue] Results are not
up to our expectations,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.460
nor are they reflective of our potential.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.350
- It was not entirely surprising

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.750
because the company had reported a string

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.140
of poor earnings and falling sales,

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.130
and so it was well known that
the company was struggling.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.990
- [Narrator] In August, cash reserves,

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.050
key for paying vendors, were still low.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.970
The company needed more cash

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.850
and was looking for a
loan to make that happen.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.340
On the 23rd, Bed Bath &amp; Beyond announced

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.160
it had secured $500 million in funding,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.550
which it hoped would help
keep shelves stocked.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.100
- Some vendors had not
been paid in months,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.290
and clearly, the company was struggling.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.660
- [Narrator] While the loan
could pay for more inventory,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.600
it wasn't enough to keep every store open.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.380
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond announced
it'd be closing 150 locations,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.660
about 20% of its doors,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.120
plus it would be starting
layoffs that amounted

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.450
to 1/5 of its corporate
and supply chain staff.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.950
Just two days later,

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:17.340
the company suffered a
different kind of loss.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.180
CFO Gustavo Arnal died by suicide.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.550
- At a time when a company
is struggling financially,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:27.870
to lose your CFO that like
that is certainly a shock,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.440
and certainly made things
even more difficult for them.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.360
- [Narrator] When second
quarter earnings were released

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.650
at the end of September,

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.660
analysts said the company was facing

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.640
yet another cash crunch.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.850
The $500 million loan had
weakened Bed Bath &amp; Beyond's

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.510
balance sheet with
liabilities exceeding assets.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.250
Still, the company felt.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.320
- [Sue] Confident that
our current liquidity

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.590
will enable the necessary strategic plans

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:53.820
we have implemented.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.050
- [Narrator] But a few weeks later,

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.180
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond announced it'd be making

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.600
a debt exchange offer where
a company exchanges bonds

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.210
for secured notes to extend maturities,

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.490
and reduce interest expenses.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.470
- The company was offering
higher interest rates

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.900
in exchange for investors taking a haircut

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.950
on their principal.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.170
- [Narrator] It meant note
holders would lose money

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.480
but they'd be guaranteed something.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.850
Stock prices dipped, then fell more

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:20.280
after Gove hosted a summit with suppliers

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.970
at the company's New Jersey
headquarters to ask for support.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.260
- She had several challenges.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.603
One, suppliers, some of
them had not been paid

00:03:27.603 --> 00:03:32.603
in months, and two, the
company had pushed out some

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.670
of these suppliers to make way
for its private label brands.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.440
Now it wanted the suppliers to come back.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.080
Well, these suppliers
had found other channels

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.040
to sell their goods.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.420
So it was taking a lot

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:45.240
of convincing to get the
suppliers back on board,

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.730
and I'm not sure they
were entirely successful.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.800
- [Narrator] These vendor
woes were all happening

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.620
before the busiest time
of the year for retailers:

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.090
the holiday season.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.520
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond was still struggling

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.000
to stock shelves just a few
days before Black Friday.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.280
Reports came out that more than 40%

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.910
of the retailer's products had
been out of stock in October.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.340
Some suppliers said they
were still owed money

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.520
and would pause shipments
until they were paid.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.290
- If you have empty
shelves, you're not going

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.030
to have people coming in and buying,

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.470
and then you're not gonna have sales,

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.300
and it becomes a vicious cycle.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.100
- [Narrator] Sales
didn't meet expectations

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.740
during the fourth quarter
and on January 5th,

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.440
Bed Bath &amp; Beyond announced
it was preparing to file

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.080
for bankruptcy in just a few weeks.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.880
A spokeswoman for Bed Bath &amp; Beyond

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.370
said it hadn't made any final decisions.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.340
And Gove said on the third
quarter earnings call.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.070
- [Sue] We are committed to
updating all stakeholders

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.860
of our plans as they develop and finalize.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.270
- [Narrator] In that earnings report,

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:45.030
the company said sales fell 33%,

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.543
and losses rose to $393 million.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.490
- [Sue] Our business was built

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.380
around our loyal customers.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:53.640
Listening and responding

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.070
to their preferences was at the center.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.080
Veering away from that path has led

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.420
to our recent financial performance.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.710
- [Narrator] The company also said

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.450
it is planning more layoffs

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.430
in an effort to cut costs.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.650
- Bankruptcy is still not a certainty

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.410
but their ability to
avoid it is shrinking.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.150
You know, there were things
they could have done,

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.820
such as sell their buybuy
BABY chain for cash.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.480
They chose not to do that, so
their options are narrowing.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.580
- [Narrator] News of an
official bankruptcy filing

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.336
could come in the next few weeks.

00:05:23.336 --> 00:05:26.003
(pensive music)

